WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:01.868
All right, so this
is the final challenge.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:02.902
[music playing]

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.437
It's a six pack of obstacles.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:07.207
NARRATOR: Caesar works with
Millie, a seven-month-old doxon

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.442
whose habit of eating
trash off the ground

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.711
could have lethal consequences.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:12.746
CAESAR: This is serious.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.047
This dog can actually get hurt.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.815
NARRATOR: Caesar's final
test will determine

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.451
if owner Britney has the
confidence to lead her

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.353
through a simulated minefield.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.688
CAESAR: Don't say a word.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.090
Just kind of guide with
energy, body language.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.492
Ready?

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.927
I don't know that she's
going to do that with me.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.129
That's not something that we--

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.463
Well, then let's
make it happen.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.065
Got to see it in your mind.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.701
I want you to remember, the most
important as you're starting,

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.735
is calmness.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.904
It's more about you
teaching yourself

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.005
to be calm, to be patient.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:39.939
Yeah.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:40.874
All right.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.576
All right, let's do it.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.211
All right.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.546
The calmness.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.814
Yeah.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.815
Ready?

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.955
Let's try this, Millie.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:56.890
Let's go.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.092
Nice.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.293
Slowly.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.761
[millie whines]

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.229
Just give a little more space.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:06.666
Not so much tension.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.667
We've talked about it.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.802
We've gone through it.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.137
So I'm aware of everything
that I need to do.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.338
CAESAR: Keep coming.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.474
But actually putting
that into motion

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:17.377
and keeping myself
in a calm state,

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:20.547
that's the thing that I'm
actually most nervous about.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.347
[millie whines]

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.315
CAESAR: A little too close.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.249
That's the obstacle there.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.751
She can't touch.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.753
Slow it down.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.621
It's stressful to walk her.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.023
[millie whines]

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.258
Remember, with the leash, the
tension should last one second,

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.626
two second the most, right?

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.661
OK.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.530
CAESAR: It's just to
direct or to stop.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.531
Relax the hand.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.036
Yes, yes.

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.338
And you have to remember
to control the nose.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:48.675
You guide the nose and
the dog will follow.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:49.943
Keep coming.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.844
Walk in the park.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.745
Walk in the park.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.014
Stop right there.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.349
Sit there.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.184
Yes.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.219
Beautiful.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.020
Right next to it.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.755
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
she's doing it.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.623
She's doing it.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.424
Come on, keep going.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.895
Mhm.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.196
Yep.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.998
Then you go.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.199
Mhm.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.503
Yeah.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:20.773
Yeah!

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.175
Yay!

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.843
I felt like a proud mother.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.180
The first time this dog has ever
attempted half of these things,

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.815
and she just did it.

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.850
Flabbergasted, actually.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:31.985
Yeah.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.186
Oh, that's the
best, right there.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.220
That was a sloppy kiss.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.022
That was a sloppy kiss, yeah.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.357
I feel pretty proud.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:41.127
Now I realize how much
my stress and anxiety

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.795
was really weighing on Millie.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:46.165
And that's such a simple
change to get Millie to stop

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.667
eating things off of
the ground, and it

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:51.271
makes me hopeful for
where we can go from here.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.239
So let's celebrate,
but wait for me.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.742
Cause I really want to
celebrate it the weenie way.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.050
I want to celebrate
the weenie way!

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:07.220
I was waiting for this day.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.923
This is the way you
celebrate with a weenie dog.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:10.857
That's right.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.792
I'm a Mexican hot dog.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.527
What do you think, Millie?

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.862
[millie whines]

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.597
This is actually the first
time I put a costume for a dog,

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:20.233
by the way, and I think
Millie deserves it.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.402
Because this case
was pretty serious.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.938
We don't want bad weenies.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.874
This is how people think of you,
by the way, the weenie dogs.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.008
Weenie dog.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:31.444
Caesar, thank you
for everything.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:35.148
I could not be more happy with
the training that you gave us.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.883
I'm not afraid to walk her.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.919
We are absolutely leaving
here today on the right path.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.853
We did it.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.487
We did it.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:41.955
Yep!

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:42.689
Yes.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:43.222
Thank you.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:43.923
Thank you!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.657
Let's go.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:45.158
All right.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:45.892
Come on.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.793
Two weenies.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.127
I hope we win an Emmy.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.963
[laughing]

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:53.766
[music playing]

